From ad4f4a3da36a5333a2fdc6cdacd8bf63111198c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:59:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show none of LiveContainer's own pages

Cartouche drives LiveContainer and the built-in SideStore without ever
showing a page of theirs. The tab bar goes: the window shows Cartouche's
console, and its System page opens over it (CartoucheRootView, which
Cartouche's prepare.sh copies in from its launcher/Sources folder), on
iOS 17 and later. An older iOS shows that Cartouche needs iOS 17, in
place of LiveContainer's app list. LiveContainer's app list and settings
no longer show anywhere.

A link opened with the app goes to Cartouche or nowhere. A pairing file
or an IPA opened from AirDrop or Files goes to Cartouche's setup or its
installer, as before. The links that led to the app list or the
settings, to install an app from a link, open a web page, launch an app
or take a certificate from another SideStore, are dropped: Cartouche
downloads no app, starts its games itself and takes the built-in
SideStore's certificate on its own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MzPJorvBGmBB88WUcRVhE7
---
 LiveContainerSwiftUI/Views/LCTabView.swift | 76 +++++-----------------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 58 deletions(-)

diff --git a/LiveContainerSwiftUI/Views/LCTabView.swift b/LiveContainerSwiftUI/Views/LCTabView.swift
index 6df405c..542251c 100644
--- a/LiveContainerSwiftUI/Views/LCTabView.swift
